From 381b7e8e8d5ba3af2aea527e014e47a772cb6df3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:17:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] state: confirm SQLITE_CORRUPT with a scoped
 read-only quick_check before the one replay
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Builds on 1a0329451e6 (rollback-guarded one-time replay). Before that replay, the writer
(_execute_write) and the pooled reader now run a bounded PRAGMA quick_check of the tables the
failing attempt touched (each table's indexes are checked with it; sqlite_schema always), on a
FRESH read-only connection in a FRESH process (new sibling module
hermes_state_corruption_confirm.py):

- scope: a SQLite authorizer installed on the connection for each attempt (TouchedTables)
  records the table NAMES every statement reads/writes at prepare time, incl. trigger bodies
  and FTS5 shadow-table statements; never SQL text or bound parameters. Unknown scope (error
  before any statement, e.g. BEGIN IMMEDIATE; an unmappable action; an attached db; a table
  the fresh connection cannot resolve) widens to a whole-file quick_check under the same bound.
- fresh process (`python -I -S`, minimal env, mode=ro + query_only): a second connection
  closed in this process would cancel every sibling's POSIX locks (howtocorrupt §2.2).
- bound: timeout = min(remaining write patience, 30s); reads 5s; <50ms left = no_budget.
- fail closed: only an exact per-table "ok" is clean. damaged / timeout / no_budget / spawn or
  child error / unparsable output latch with no replay, reason carries confirm=<outcome>
  scope=<tables> <elapsed>.
- a clean check allows exactly ONE replay; a recurrence latches without a second check.
  Clean-then-replayed errors are counted (hermes_state_health.note_unconfirmed_corruption /
  unconfirmed_corruption_count) and logged "NOT confirmed (confirm=clean scope=...)".
- unchanged: FTS provenance first (FTS-scoped faults never reach the check), stage / rollback /
  page-cache blockers, COMMIT never replayed (no check either), durable-commit-then-error
  applies once.

Known costs (deliberate, per card acceptance #4): a scoped check of a multi-GB table, or the
whole-file check for a BEGIN-stage error, can exceed the patience bound and then latches
(= pre-1a0329451e6 behaviour on that path). Installing the authorizer per attempt expires the
connection's prepared statements, so statements re-prepare once per write/pooled read.

Five whys (selfheal gateway-d7a592a91c), corrected from 1a0329451e6:
Problem: 2026-11-03 16:26-17:01 PT every state.db write on hermes-hub refused with
  StateDbCorruptError (gateway.log.3:6085-6134); 2 worker runs crashed.
Why 1: _raise_if_db_corrupt(storage=True) refuses every write once the process-wide flag is
  set — evidence: hermes_state.py _raise_if_db_corrupt.
Why 2: the flag was set by one SQLITE_CORRUPT at 00:01:06Z and never re-checked — evidence:
  hermes_state_health.mark_storage_corrupt keeps the first error.
Why 3: any bare SQLITE_CORRUPT without FTS provenance counted as structural with no
  confirmation step — evidence: is_structural_corruption_error -> _halt_db_corrupt on origin/main.
Why 4 (corrected): the cause of the first error is UNDETERMINED. A later per-table
  quick_check passing on all 36 tables + 8 FTS tables, and 20,900+ messages saved after the
  restart, show the file read back consistent THEN; they do not prove it was never damaged
  (a page could have been rewritten since), nor identify the fault (misread, transient I/O,
  since-replaced page are hypotheses; 00:01 logs rotated). Evidence boundary: no capture of
  the failing page / statement at the time.
Root (happened): design assumed "corrupt once, corrupt forever" — no confirmation step, restart
  the only exit, and nothing recorded which tables the failing statement touched.
Root (not caught): test_storage_health_latch.py only injected persistent damage; no test
  injected a one-shot error, and the latch reason kept only the message text.
Recurrence: first false-positive latch since bd945ec3845 (#120274).
Countermeasures:
- symptom/root: scoped read-only confirm + one replay — proof:
  tests/hermes_state/test_storage_corruption_scoped_confirm.py; RED with hermes_state.py at
  1a0329451e6: 18 fail (clean-confirm replay x3 entry paths, recurrence x3, timeout x3,
  error x3, no_budget, real damaged B-tree, begin-stage full scope, 3 pooled-read); GREEN 26/26.
- safety: mutant "ignore confirm result + unscoped" fails 11 (timeout/error x3 paths, no_budget,
  damaged B-tree, clean-confirm scope x3); FTS bypass / COMMIT fault / durable-commit guards and
  all 15 tests of test_storage_corruption_confirmation.py stay green.
- detection: reason/log carry confirm outcome, scope, elapsed; unconfirmed count per db.
- deferred: proposal's coach rule on "unconfirmed corruption" (card t_01a1a5a82366d7e6).
